    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe your issue\n\nSo I am not sure what are the reasons for this, but this was a surprise:\n```python\ndef foo(s):\n    MASK = (1 << len(s)) - 1\n```\nMASK has automatically become `Py_ssize_t` type and caused issues.\n\nThis is the only case that I know of that does C typing for you without asking (in Pure Python mode at least).\n\nIs this intentional?\nAre there reasons for this?",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> MASK has automatically become Py_ssize_t type and caused issues.\n\nWhat issues?\n\n`len(s)` definitely returns a `Py_ssize_t` so that's correct. The expression as a whole is more complicated to reason about because it might overflow, but doesn't look obviously wrong to me.\n\n> This is the only case that I know of that does C typing for you without asking (in Pure Python mode at least).\n\nThere's actually quite a bit of automatic type inference happening (just as an example, `{}.has_key(...)` will return a boolean-like type. It should typically be in cases where it doesn't cause noticeable differences.",
